  "1": {
   "segId": "Shabbat.21b.2",
   "sugya": "shabbat_21a_petilot_chanukka",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "objection",
     "object": "obj_veha_gamra",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "והא גמרה! -- but he did learn it",
     "against": "p_abaye_i_zachai",
     "state": "answered"
    },
    {
     "type": "objection_answer",
     "object": "ans_girsa_deyankuta",
     "gloss_en": "נפקא מינה לגירסא דינקותא -- the difference is for the learning of one's youth",
     "answers": "obj_veha_gamra",
     "restores": "p_abaye_i_zachai"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_abaye_i_zachai",
     "gloss_en": "Abaye: had I merited, I would have learned this teaching from the start"
    }
   ]
  },
  "2": {
   "segId": "Shabbat.21b.3",
   "sugya": "shabbat_21a_petilot_chanukka",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "objection",
     "object": "obj_rominhu_mitzvata",
     "kind": "tanya",
     "gloss_en": "וכבתה אין זקוק לה? ורמינהו: מצותה משתשקע החמה עד שתכלה רגל מן השוק -- מאי לאו, דאי כבתה הדר מדליק לה!",
     "against": "p_kavta_ein_zakuk",
     "state": "answered"
    },
    {
     "type": "objection_answer",
     "object": "ans_ii_lo_adlik",
     "gloss_en": "לא, דאי לא אדליק -- מדליק: if he has not yet lit, he may still light [until then]",
     "answers": "obj_rominhu_mitzvata",
     "restores": "p_kavta_ein_zakuk"
    },
    {
     "type": "objection_answer",
     "object": "ans_leshiura",
     "gloss_en": "ואי נמי לשיעורה -- alternatively, [the baraita gives] its measure",
     "answers": "obj_rominhu_mitzvata",
     "restores": "p_kavta_ein_zakuk"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_baraita_mitzvata",
     "gloss_en": "its mitzva is from sunset until feet cease from the market"
    }
   ]
  },
  "11": {
   "segId": "Shabbat.21b.12",
   "sugya": "shabbat_21b_mai_chanukah",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_zot_omeret_betoch_asara",
     "kind": "dika_nami",
     "gloss_en": "זאת אומרת: since R' Yehuda exempts the storekeeper's Hanukkah lamp, it must belong within ten; דאי סלקא דעתך למעלה מעשרה, לימא ליה: היה לך להניח למעלה מגמל ורוכבו -- were above ten permitted, the camel-owner could say: you should have placed it above the camel and its rider",
     "supports": "p_betoch_asara",
     "status": "rejected"
    },
    {
     "type": "support_deflection",
     "object": "defl_mitrecha_tuva",
     "gloss_en": "ודילמא: אי מיטרחא ליה טובא אתי לאימנועי ממצוה -- perhaps R' Yehuda exempts because, if he is troubled too much, he will come to refrain from the mitzva; the exemption then shows nothing about the height",
     "deflects": "s_zot_omeret_betoch_asara",
     "refuted": false
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_ryehuda_ner_chanukah_patur",
     "gloss_en": "R' Yehuda: with a Hanukkah lamp [put outside] -- [the storekeeper] is exempt"
    }
   ]
  },
